---
import site from '../content/site.json';
---

<div class="pricing-note">
  <div class="heading">How pricing works</div>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <span class="bullet">•</span>
      <p><strong>${site.minimumVisit} minimum per visit</strong> — not a price per room or per item. Booked alone, a small job (like a single room, or one recliner) lands on ${site.minimumVisit} because that&rsquo;s the visit minimum, not because that&rsquo;s what the item costs. Add a second thing and you&rsquo;re not paying that minimum twice or stacking the list prices — you&rsquo;re paying for the actual combined job.</p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <span class="bullet">•</span>
      <p><strong>A &ldquo;room&rdquo; is up to {site.roomDefinitionSqFt} sq ft.</strong> Larger open areas count as two.</p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <span class="bullet">•</span>
      <p><strong>Every price here is an estimate.</strong> I try to be as transparent as I can with these numbers, but your home isn&rsquo;t a spreadsheet — the firm price I give you before any work starts is the one that counts, and it won&rsquo;t change unless you ask for more.</p>
    </li>
  </ul>
</div>

<style>
  .pricing-note {
    margin-top: 20px;
    background: var(--ff-surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--ff-border);
    border-radius: var(--ff-radius-inner);
    padding: 24px 26px;
  }

  .heading {
    font-family: var(--ff-font-display);
    font-weight: var(--ff-weight-semibold);
    font-size: 17px;
    color: var(--ff-navy);
    letter-spacing: var(--ff-tracking-tight);
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }

  ul {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 13px;
  }

  li {
    display: flex;
    gap: 11px;
  }

  .bullet {
    color: var(--ff-azure);
    font-weight: var(--ff-weight-bold);
    font-size: var(--ff-size-body-sm);
    line-height: 1.55;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  p {
    font-size: var(--ff-size-body-sm);
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--ff-text-body);
    margin: 0;
  }

  strong {
    color: var(--ff-text);
    font-weight: var(--ff-weight-bold);
  }

  .warning {
    color: var(--ff-warning);
    font-weight: var(--ff-weight-semibold);
  }
</style>
